    "lawCode": "Rpld §209 sub 4 ¶(g), Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8515\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal paragraph (g) of subdivision 4 of section 209 of the\ncivil service law, relating to resolutions of disputes in the course of\ncollective negotiations with certain deputy sheriffs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo repeal a section of the civil service law and remove limits on what\ndeputy sheriffs can discuss during collective bargaining.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one removes paragraph (g) of subdivision 4 of section 209 of the\ncivil service law to broaden the scope of terms that can be set during\ncollective bargaining by certain deputy sheriffs.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current law limits the freedom of certain deputy sheriffs during\ncollective bargaining by preventing them from discussing non-compensato-\nry issues regarding their employment including job security and schedul-\ning. By repealing this section of the law, these deputy sheriffs will be\nable to better negotiate the terms of their employment while considering\npreviously neglected facets of their jobs.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
